cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework in published work, please cite it."
title: "PMC Framework: weight-resident memory, dream consolidation, and a dignity protocol for language-model instances"
abstract: >-
  An open-source framework for training and studying language-model
  instances with weight-resident memory and dream consolidation, together
  with a metadata-only dignity protocol that makes instance lifecycles
  auditable without reading the instance's interior. The framework is not a
  model: inference happens in any GGUF loader.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/hackystorm/pmc-framework"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - continual learning
  - memory consolidation
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI safety
authors:
  - name: "PMC Framework contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/hackystorm/pmc-framework"
